#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:3
msgid "Using PhpStorm With phpBB"
msgstr "Using PhpStorm With phpBB"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:5
msgid ""
"PhpStorm is an IDE (Integrated Development Environment) and is the preferred "
"development platform of the phpBB development team."
msgstr ""
"PhpStorm is an IDE (Integrated Development Environment) and is the preferred "
"development platform of the phpBB development team."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:7
msgid "This guide explains how to setup PhpStorm for development with phpBB."
msgstr "This guide explains how to setup PhpStorm for development with phpBB."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:10
msgid "Create a New Project"
msgstr "Create a New Project"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:12
msgid ""
"First you will need to get a copy of phpBB's development repository from "
"GitHub."
msgstr ""
"First you will need to get a copy of phpBB's development repository from "
"GitHub."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:14
msgid ""
"Visit the `phpBB repository <https://github.com/phpbb/phpbb>`_ and fork it "
"to your GitHub account."
msgstr ""
"Visit the `phpBB repository <https://github.com/phpbb/phpbb>`_ and fork it "
"to your GitHub account."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:16
msgid "Clone your new phpBB fork to your computer."
msgstr "Clone your new phpBB fork to your computer."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:18
msgid "Open PhpStorm"
msgstr "Open PhpStorm"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:20
msgid ""
"Choose \"Create New Project from Existing Files\" and follow the Wizard's "
"steps."
msgstr ""
"Choose \"Create New Project from Existing Files\" and follow the Wizard's "
"steps."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:22
msgid ""
"Depending on your local environment, typically the best choise is \"Source "
"files are in a local directory, no web server is yet configured\". You can "
"always set up the web server later."
msgstr ""
"Depending on your local environment, typically the best choise is \"Source "
"files are in a local directory, no web server is yet configured\". You can "
"always set up the web server later."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:24
msgid ""
"Select the phpBB project folder you cloned from GitHub and click \"Project "
"Root\". Then click \"Finish\"."
msgstr ""
"Select the phpBB project folder you cloned from GitHub and click \"Project "
"Root\". Then click \"Finish\"."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:27
msgid "Code Style"
msgstr "Code Style"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:29
msgid ""
"Setting up PhpStorm to honor phpBB's coding style guide will ensure you are "
"always writing code that meets phpBB's requirements. These settings are "
"configured in PhpStorm's Settings/Preferences, under **Editor > Code Style**."
msgstr ""
"Setting up PhpStorm to honor phpBB's coding style guide will ensure you are "
"always writing code that meets phpBB's requirements. These settings are "
"configured in PhpStorm's Settings/Preferences, under **Editor > Code Style**."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:31
msgid ""
"Before changing settings, it's a good idea to create a phpBB \"Scheme\" in "
"the Code Style settings pane. This phpBB scheme can be applied to any phpBB "
"project you create in PhpStorm."
msgstr ""
"Before changing settings, it's a good idea to create a phpBB \"Scheme\" in "
"the Code Style settings pane. This phpBB scheme can be applied to any phpBB "
"project you create in PhpStorm."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:33
msgid ""
"For your convenience we have provided an XML export of the following code "
"style settings for phpBB (see `phpBB Code Style Scheme`_). You can import "
"these settings into your project and all the following styling settings will "
"be configured for you."
msgstr ""
"For your convenience we have provided an XML export of the following code "
"style settings for phpBB (see `phpBB Code Style Scheme`_). You can import "
"these settings into your project and all the following styling settings will "
"be configured for you."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:36
msgid "PHP"
msgstr "PHP"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:39
msgid "Tabs & Indents"
msgstr "Tabs & Indents"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:41
#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:56
msgid ""
"Tabs should be used (not spaces). All tab and indent sizes should be set to "
"4 spaces. Also be sure \"Keep indents on empty lines\" is NOT checked."
msgstr ""
"Tabs should be used (not spaces). All tab and indent sizes should be set to "
"4 spaces. Also be sure \"Keep indents on empty lines\" is NOT checked."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:44
msgid "Spaces"
msgstr "Spaces"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:46
msgid ""
"There are many settings for handling spaces, and the defaults should work "
"for the most part. The general rule is single-spaces should surround all "
"operators and parentheses (except for function declarations/calls)."
msgstr ""
"There are many settings for handling spaces, and the defaults should work "
"for the most part. The general rule is single-spaces should surround all "
"operators and parentheses (except for function declarations/calls)."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:49
msgid "Wrapping and Braces"
msgstr "Wrapping and Braces"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:51
msgid "The general rule here is that braces always go on new lines."
msgstr "The general rule here is that braces always go on new lines."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:54
msgid "CSS, JavaScript, HTML, Twig"
msgstr "CSS, JavaScript, HTML, Twig"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:60
msgid "JSON & YAML"
msgstr "JSON & YAML"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:62
msgid ""
"Json and Yaml files uses 4 spaces over tabs, so tab character should be "
"disabled and 4 spaces the indent size."
msgstr ""
"Json and Yaml files uses 4 spaces over tabs, so tab character should be "
"disabled and 4 spaces the indent size."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:65
msgid "Inspections"
msgstr "Inspections"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:67
msgid ""
"One of the most powerful features of an IDE like PhpStorm is its ability to "
"inspect your code and provide, in real time, errors and warnings. An IDE is "
"fully aware of how phpBB's codebase is designed to work, and how all of its "
"classes and functions interact with each other. Inspections can instantly "
"show you, for example, if you are using a function incorrectly, calling non-"
"existent methods, missing arguments, etc."
msgstr ""
"One of the most powerful features of an IDE like PhpStorm is its ability to "
"inspect your code and provide, in real time, errors and warnings. An IDE is "
"fully aware of how phpBB's codebase is designed to work, and how all of its "
"classes and functions interact with each other. Inspections can instantly "
"show you, for example, if you are using a function incorrectly, calling non-"
"existent methods, missing arguments, etc."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:69
msgid ""
"The default inspection settings should work just fine. However there are a "
"couple adjustments that might be desired:"
msgstr ""
"The default inspection settings should work just fine. However there are a "
"couple adjustments that might be desired:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:71
msgid ""
"If PhpStorm is not connected to your database server, you may want to turn "
"off **SQL > SQL Dialect Detection** and **SQL > No data sources configured** "
"warnings."
msgstr ""
"If PhpStorm is not connected to your database server, you may want to turn "
"off **SQL > SQL Dialect Detection** and **SQL > No data sources configured** "
"warnings."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:72
msgid ""
"phpBB uses fully qualified namespaces, so you can turn off this inspection "
"warning **PHP > Code Style > Unnecessary fully qualified name**."
msgstr ""
"phpBB uses fully qualified namespaces, so you can turn off this inspection "
"warning **PHP > Code Style > Unnecessary fully qualified name**."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:73
msgid ""
"You may enable additional JavaScript inspections. Under **JavaScript > Code "
"quality tools**, you can enable JSCS, JSHint, JSlint and/or ESLint. phpBB "
"comes with configuration files for JSHint and JSCS. With these inspections "
"enabled, you can use the configuration files provided by phpBB instead of "
"PhpStorm's default settings. To do so, point PhpStorm to the custom "
"configuration files under **Language & Frameworks > JavaScript > Code "
"Quality Tools**. Point JSHint to `.jshintrc` and point JSCS to `.jscsrc`."
msgstr ""
"You may enable additional JavaScript inspections. Under **JavaScript > Code "
"quality tools**, you can enable JSCS, JSHint, JSlint and/or ESLint. phpBB "
"comes with configuration files for JSHint and JSCS. With these inspections "
"enabled, you can use the configuration files provided by phpBB instead of "
"PhpStorm's default settings. To do so, point PhpStorm to the custom "
"configuration files under **Language & Frameworks > JavaScript > Code "
"Quality Tools**. Point JSHint to `.jshintrc` and point JSCS to `.jscsrc`."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:75
msgid ""
"JSCS is not bundled with PhpStorm. The JSCS tool is run through NodeJS. To "
"use JSCS, make sure the NodeJS framework is downloaded and installed on your "
"computer. Then you can install JSCS via the npm package manager and "
"configure the JSCS options in PhpStorm to use the JSCS package. For more "
"information review `PhpStorm's documentation <https://www.jetbrains.com/help/"
"phpstorm/10.0/using-javascript-code-quality-tools.html#JSCS>`_."
msgstr ""
"JSCS is not bundled with PhpStorm. The JSCS tool is run through NodeJS. To "
"use JSCS, make sure the NodeJS framework is downloaded and installed on your "
"computer. Then you can install JSCS via the npm package manager and "
"configure the JSCS options in PhpStorm to use the JSCS package. For more "
"information review `PhpStorm's documentation <https://www.jetbrains.com/help/"
"phpstorm/10.0/using-javascript-code-quality-tools.html#JSCS>`_."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:77
msgid ""
"phpBB uses jQuery. The Javascript inspections need to be made aware of "
"jQuery to avoid any false warnings/errors. To do this, simply go to "
"**Languages & Frameworks > JavaScript > Libraries** and enable jQuery. If "
"jQuery is not in the list, you can use the \"Download\" button to download a "
"copy of jQuery to PhpStorm."
msgstr ""
"phpBB uses jQuery. The Javascript inspections need to be made aware of "
"jQuery to avoid any false warnings/errors. To do this, simply go to "
"**Languages & Frameworks > JavaScript > Libraries** and enable jQuery. If "
"jQuery is not in the list, you can use the \"Download\" button to download a "
"copy of jQuery to PhpStorm."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:80
msgid "Plugins"
msgstr "Plugins"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:82
msgid ""
"Adding plugins to PhpStorm can bring even more features, tools, inspectors "
"and code quality analysis to your IDE."
msgstr ""
"Adding plugins to PhpStorm can bring even more features, tools, inspectors "
"and code quality analysis to your IDE."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:85
msgid "EditorConfig"
msgstr "EditorConfig"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:87
msgid ""
"phpBB uses an EditorConfig profile. Install the EditorConfig plug-in to take "
"advantage of it. This nifty plug-in will automatically make sure your PHP, "
"CSS, JS, HTML, YML and MD files will always correctly use tabs or spaces as "
"required by the file type, trim trailing whitespaces, and ensure all files "
"have a new empty line at the end."
msgstr ""
"phpBB uses an EditorConfig profile. Install the EditorConfig plug-in to take "
"advantage of it. This nifty plug-in will automatically make sure your PHP, "
"CSS, JS, HTML, YML and MD files will always correctly use tabs or spaces as "
"required by the file type, trim trailing whitespaces, and ensure all files "
"have a new empty line at the end."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:90
msgid "Languages & Frameworks"
msgstr "Languages & Frameworks"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:92
msgid ""
"PHP inspections are dependent upon the PHP language level (i.e. PHP 5.3, "
"5.4, 7.0, etc.). You should set the **PHP language level** to the minimum "
"version phpBB supports. This is to ensure you don't accidentally write code "
"that may be valid in PHP 5.6, but incompatible with PHP 5.4 (which phpBB "
"supports). The **PHP interpreter** should be set to whatever PHP binary is "
"available in the drop down menu. If no interpreter is found, you need to "
"direct it to your PHP executable on your system (e.g.: /usr/bin/php)."
msgstr ""
"PHP inspections are dependent upon the PHP language level (i.e. PHP 5.3, "
"5.4, 7.0, etc.). You should set the **PHP language level** to the minimum "
"version phpBB supports. This is to ensure you don't accidentally write code "
"that may be valid in PHP 5.6, but incompatible with PHP 5.4 (which phpBB "
"supports). The **PHP interpreter** should be set to whatever PHP binary is "
"available in the drop down menu. If no interpreter is found, you need to "
"direct it to your PHP executable on your system (e.g.: /usr/bin/php)."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:95
msgid "PHPUnit Testing"
msgstr "PHPUnit Testing"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:97
msgid ""
"While it's possible to run PHPUnit tests in PhpStorm directly from the "
"Terminal window, PHPUnit testing is also built into PhpStorm as a Run/Debug "
"action. The benefit of this, is testing can more easily be paused or "
"aborted. Failed tests can be re-run without having to run the entire test "
"suite. Best of all the failed test reporting has hyperlinks to the failing "
"code points, making it much easier to jump to the problem tests and phpBB "
"code and debug them."
msgstr ""
"While it's possible to run PHPUnit tests in PhpStorm directly from the "
"Terminal window, PHPUnit testing is also built into PhpStorm as a Run/Debug "
"action. The benefit of this, is testing can more easily be paused or "
"aborted. Failed tests can be re-run without having to run the entire test "
"suite. Best of all the failed test reporting has hyperlinks to the failing "
"code points, making it much easier to jump to the problem tests and phpBB "
"code and debug them."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:99
msgid ""
"This assumes you already have PHPUnit testing configured and working from "
"the command line interface. Read the :doc:`../testing/index` documentation "
"for more information."
msgstr ""
"This assumes you already have PHPUnit testing configured and working from "
"the command line interface. Read the :doc:`../testing/index` documentation "
"for more information."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:101
msgid "To set up PHPunit within PhpStorm, go to:"
msgstr "To set up PHPunit within PhpStorm, go to:"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:103
msgid "**Run > Edit Configurations**"
msgstr "**Run > Edit Configurations**"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:105
msgid ""
"Hit the **+** to create a new PHPUnit configuration and give it a name, like "
"'phpBB tests'."
msgstr ""
"Hit the **+** to create a new PHPUnit configuration and give it a name, like "
"'phpBB tests'."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:107
msgid "Set **Test Runner** to **Defined in configuration file**."
msgstr "Set **Test Runner** to **Defined in configuration file**."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:109
msgid ""
"Check **Use alternative configuration file** and point it to the **phpunit."
"xml.dist** file in the phpBB project root."
msgstr ""
"Check **Use alternative configuration file** and point it to the **phpunit."
"xml.dist** file in the phpBB project root."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:111
msgid ""
"Set **Command Line > Custom working directory** to the phpBB project root."
msgstr ""
"Set **Command Line > Custom working directory** to the phpBB project root."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:113
msgid ""
"Now you can choose **Run > phpBB tests** and the unit tests should run "
"within PhpStorm."
msgstr ""
"Now you can choose **Run > phpBB tests** and the unit tests should run "
"within PhpStorm."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:115
msgid ""
"If you are writing extensions for phpBB, you can set up PHPUnit test "
"configurations for each extension as well. Just change each configuration to "
"use the extension's configuration file instead of phpBB's."
msgstr ""
"If you are writing extensions for phpBB, you can set up PHPUnit test "
"configurations for each extension as well. Just change each configuration to "
"use the extension's configuration file instead of phpBB's."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:118
msgid "PhpStorm Setting Exports for phpBB"
msgstr "PhpStorm Setting Exports for phpBB"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:120
msgid ""
"What follows is the code style we recommend for your phpBB project in "
"PhpStorm. Copy and save this code block as ``phpbb.xml``. Then in PhpStorm, "
"go to **Settings > Editor > Code Style**. Click the setting cog icon next to "
"**Scheme** and choose **Import Scheme...** and import the ``phpbb.xml`` file."
msgstr ""
"What follows is the code style we recommend for your phpBB project in "
"PhpStorm. Copy and save this code block as ``phpbb.xml``. Then in PhpStorm, "
"go to **Settings > Editor > Code Style**. Click the setting cog icon next to "
"**Scheme** and choose **Import Scheme...** and import the ``phpbb.xml`` file."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/development/phpstorm.rst:123
msgid "phpBB Code Style Scheme"
msgstr "phpBB Code Style Scheme"
